The exercise was implemented:
Generating a few different clock frequency as output(50MHz, 84MHz and 120 MHz) using the PLL engine with the HSI as the source to the PLL.

Summary:
1. A new function was created SystemClockConfig(uint8_t clock_freq) that would do the following
  1.1 Configure the oscillator and the clock with the source as HSI
  1.2 Configure the PLL engine - update the dividers M and P and the multiplier N based on clock_freq which is the desired clock frequency 
  1.3 Updated the HAL functions for the oscillator and clock inits : HAL_RCC_OscConfig(&osc_init) and HAL_RCC_ClockConfig(&clk_init, FLatency)
  1.4 Updates the Systick timer via the 
      1.4.1 HAL_SYSTICK_Config(HAL_RCC_GetHCLKFreq()/1000)- updates the ticks based on the HCLK frequency
      1.4.2 HAL_SYSTICK_CLKSourceConfig(SYSTICK_CLKSOURCE_HCLK); - configures the clock source for the systick timer which is the AHB clock

2. In the main.c
  2.1 Calls the HAL_Init() which picks the definition of the MSP_Init from the stm32f4xx_hal_msp.c
  2.2 Call the UART2_Init()
  2.3 Transmit the information about the clock via the UART
  2.4 Call the SystemClockConfig()
  2.5 Call the UART2_Init() to configure the peripheral as per the PLL clock frequency from step 2.4
  2.6 Transmit the information again

3. Setup the tera term with a baud rate as 115200 and check the output



 
